# Stack

The libraries this service uses, and the ones it must not. Versions live in
`pyproject.toml` (and `uv.lock`) only.

## Approved

| Purpose | Library | Why |
|---|---|---|
| HTTP API | FastAPI on uvicorn | async, typed dependencies, OpenAPI for meal-platform `contracts/` |
| Boundary models | Pydantic v2 | validation and JSON at the edges (see [models.md](conventions/models.md)) |
| Configuration | pydantic-settings | typed settings from environment variables (see [settings.md](conventions/settings.md)) |
| Logging | structlog, through `observability` | JSON lines with trace ids, the same records exported to Loki |
| Outgoing HTTP | httpx2 (`HttpClientDep`) | async, maintained successor of httpx, traced by OpenTelemetry |
| Telemetry | OpenTelemetry SDK, OTLP exporter, FastAPI and httpx instrumentation | traces, metrics and logs into meal-platform's Grafana |
{%- if with_database %}
| Database | SQLAlchemy 2 (async) + asyncpg + Alembic, SQLAlchemy instrumentation | typed async ORM, a native asyncio PostgreSQL driver, migrations (see [persistence.md](conventions/persistence.md)) |
{%- else %}
| Database | none here; the template's `with_database` option adds SQLAlchemy 2 (async) + asyncpg + Alembic | ask before adding a database |
{%- endif %}
{%- if with_cache %}
| Cache | Valkey through redis-py (`redis.asyncio`), redis instrumentation | the client with OpenTelemetry support; an optional cache (see [caching.md](conventions/caching.md)) |
{%- else %}
| Cache | none here; the template's `with_cache` option adds Valkey through redis-py | ask before adding a cache |
{%- endif %}
| Tests | pytest, pytest-asyncio, pytest-cov{% if with_database or with_cache %}, testcontainers{% endif %} | see [testing.md](conventions/testing.md) |
| Quality | ruff, pyright (strict), import-linter, pre-commit | `make check` |
| Packaging | uv, uv_build | one lock file, fast installs, the Docker image builds with it |

## Banned

| Don't use | Use instead | Enforced by |
|---|---|---|
| `requests`, `aiohttp`, `httpx` | httpx2 through the shared client | ruff (`banned-api`) |
| `logging.getLogger`, `print` | `get_logger` from `{{ package_name }}.observability` | ruff (`banned-api`, `T20`) |
| `typing.Optional`, `Union`, `List`, `Dict` | `X \| None`, `X \| Y`, `list`, `dict` | ruff (`banned-api`, `UP`) |
| Tortoise ORM, other ORMs, sync database drivers | SQLAlchemy 2 async + asyncpg | review |
| `dependency-injector`, `fastapi-class`, `fastapi-utils` | FastAPI dependencies and the providers in `api/dependencies.py` | review |
| `valkey` (valkey-py), `valkey-glide` | redis-py: valkey-py has no OpenTelemetry instrumentation, GLIDE's can't join the app's traces | review |
| Celery, stream consumers, background workers | nothing in the template; services talk over HTTP. Messaging needs its own decision first | review |
| Poetry, pip, pip-tools | `uv add` / `uv add --dev` | review |

Authentication libraries are not chosen yet; that decision comes with the first service
that needs it.

## Adding a dependency

A new runtime dependency needs approval first (see "Boundaries for agents" in `AGENTS.md`).
Then: `uv add <package>` (`uv add --dev` for tools), a lower bound that matches the version
you tested, and a row in the table above with the reason. If it does I/O, it needs
OpenTelemetry instrumentation or manual spans.
